Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.15.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.15.0 targets the remaining one-frame flash on every app switch (both directions). Archive 15 pins down two new facts. First, on this device FBScene.foreground cannot be read through key-value coding (the archive shows fg=n(0) on every single health line), so the preventive-tier delta detection for foreground never fired and setForeground:YES was never sent by the preventive tier; what actually rescued every one of the 23 black episodes was the unconditional foreground=YES inside the level-1 real-black recovery write, always 200 to 400 ms late because the layers must vanish before the watchdog notices. Second, 45 of the 48 real-black episodes happened while deactivationReasons was still 0: on an app switch the system drops the scene layers outright, with no warning sign, and a 200 ms poller can never get ahead of that. 0.15.0 therefore works on two fronts. On the write side, the preventive tier now treats setForeground:YES as a keep-alive item: when the value cannot be read it is sent every preventive tick (pure state item, no geometry), and the read-back verification becomes tri-state so that unreadable no longer counts as a failure (previously three unreadable ticks would fuse the switch off and also disable it inside the real-black recovery, dangerously close to the permanent-black behavior of 0.12.0). On the visual side, three zero-side-effect changes hide the 200 to 400 ms window itself: the presenter context backgroundColorWhileNotHosting is set to clear (the archive dump shows BGColorWhileHosting = gray 0 alpha 1, pure black - that is the color painted during the window), the presentation view background (including its internal backgroundView) is stripped, and a snapshot of the last healthy frame is padded underneath the content area, refreshed at most every two seconds while healthy. When the layers drop, the user sees the frozen last frame instead of black. New config key: keepAliveSnapshot = true (set false to isolate the snapshot from the transparency changes). Config version migrates 15 to 16.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
